SleelaTerminal(TM) — original shell
===================================

SleelaTerminal(TM) is an ORIGINAL command shell authored by the SLeeLa project.
The code in this directory (sleela-terminal/) is clean-room work: it was written
from scratch by SLeeLa, guided by public shell *specifications* and the *ideas*
common to POSIX shells, not by copying any existing shell's source code.

Authorship
----------

  SleelaTerminal(TM) shell
  Copyright (C) The SLeeLa project.

All source, headers, docs, and tests under sleela-terminal/ are SLeeLa's own
work and carry the SleelaTerminal(TM) identity.

Not derived from GNU Bash
-------------------------

SleelaTerminal(TM) is NOT a fork of, and does NOT incorporate source from, GNU
Bash or any other GPL-licensed shell. Where SleelaTerminal(TM) behaves like a
POSIX shell (pipelines, redirections, quoting, control flow, arithmetic), that
is because it targets the same *observable behaviour* described by public
specifications — behaviour and interfaces are not themselves copyrightable, but
source code is, and none was taken.

Relationship to the vendored Bash tree
---------------------------------------

The repository also vendors GNU Bash under bash/ as a separate, unmodified
component (see bash/NOTICE). That tree remains the work of the Free Software
Foundation under the GPL and is entirely distinct from this original shell.
SleelaTerminal(TM)'s product branding (bash/SLEELATERMINAL.md) documents how the
product may be *built on* GNU Bash; sleela-terminal/ is instead SLeeLa's own
from-scratch shell implementation.

In short: brand what you authored. This is authored.
